@startuml runtime-01-fanout-read
' Runtime scenario 1 - a fan-out read.
' Canonical source for docs/architecture/arc42.md section 6.1.
' Example: evm wallet balance WALLET -c base,mainnet
' contract owner, contract code and contract proxy-info follow the same shape and
' differ only in what they do inside the loop.

title Runtime scenario 1 - fan-out read (evm wallet balance)

actor Operator
participant "index.ts" as Boot
participant "src/cli/wallet.ts" as Def
participant "balance handler" as H
participant "lib/chains" as Ch
participant "lib/rpc" as Rpc
participant "JSON-RPC endpoint" as Node
participant "lib/prices" as Px

Operator -> Boot: evm wallet balance 0x... -c base,mainnet
activate Boot
Boot -> Boot: loadEnv() - ./.env then the config directory .env,\nonce, never overwriting a set variable
note right of Boot
  Loaded here rather than per handler.
  Thirteen of twenty-one handlers used to
  call it and eight did not, so a variable
  set only in a .env file was visible to
  some commands and invisible to others.
end note
Boot -> Def: program.parseAsync()
activate Def
Def -> Def: parser rejects conflicting options (-c with -xc)
Def -> H: balanceCommand(wallet, options)
deactivate Def
activate H

H -> H: resolveAddress() - address, private key, or\nthe name of a variable holding either
H -> Ch: loadProfile(options.profile)
activate Ch
note right of Ch
  Throws. A missing or malformed profile
  leaves nothing to fan out over.
end note
Ch --> H: RpcProfile
deactivate Ch
H -> Ch: selectChains(-c, -xc, profile)
activate Ch
Ch --> H: ordered chain names
deactivate Ch

loop for each chain, sequentially
  H -> Ch: resolveChain(name, profile)
  activate Ch
  note right of Ch
    Never throws. Six distinct failures
    become a populated error field:
    not in profile, no chain_id, no rpc_url,
    unresolved environment reference,
    malformed URL, unreachable endpoint.
  end note
  Ch --> H: ResolvedChain
  deactivate Ch

  alt endpoint resolved
    H -> Rpc: createProvider(endpoint, chainId)
    activate Rpc
    Rpc --> H: JsonRpcProvider, chain id pinned by staticNetwork
    deactivate Rpc
    H -> Node: eth_getBalance and eth_getTransactionCount(pending),\nunder one Promise.all
    activate Node
    Node --> H: results, or a throw caught into result.error
    deactivate Node
    H -> H: provider.destroy() in finally
  else no endpoint
    H -> H: push a placeholder row carrying the error,\nwith balance, balanceEth and nonce as zeros
  end
end

H -> Px: resolvePriceSource().getNativeUsdPrices(distinct chains)
activate Px
note right of Px
  One batched request for the whole run,
  after the loop, 5 s timeout.
  Never throws: a failure yields no prices.
end note
Px --> H: Map of chain id to price or null
deactivate Px

H -> Operator: table on stdout, or JSON with a per-row error field
note left of H
  Exit 0 even when every chain failed.
  A script must read the rows, not the
  exit code - and the zeroed placeholder
  means summing balanceEth without
  checking error under-counts silently.
end note
deactivate H
deactivate Boot

@enduml
